From 4649e5c225c6ef3c2ac377929e85ea752e43f3d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Manuel Lopez Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 12:59:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 130/130] config: regenerate the defconfig - it was missing
 codec, PCIe, VPU and joydev
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The config commits after Jul 13 modified .config (a local build artifact)
instead of the versioned defconfig, which is the one published in the bundle
and the one used by anyone rebuilding by the README.

Result: the published defconfig produced a kernel WITHOUT analog audio
(SND_SUN55I_A523_CODEC), WITHOUT PCIe (PCIE_SUN55I_RC + AW_INNO_COMBOPHY),
WITHOUT VPU (VIDEO_SUNXI_CEDAR_VE) and without joydev/uinput - exactly the
advertised features.

Regenerated with 'make savedefconfig' from the board-validated .config;
verified that it reproduces that .config exactly (0 differences).

Found by an automatic audit of the series.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/opi4a_blindboot_defconfig
index 49326a282..fe0bcb74e 100644
